# Decimal multiplication with double operands

Multiplies 1.20 by 2.25 in both operand orders to verify the f64 value
converts into an exact decimal result, producing 2.7000 either way.

>>> source
double_value: double = 2.25
decimal_left: decimal = 1.20

// Verifies the Decimal/Double conversion with the double operand first.
double_times_decimal: decimal = double_value * decimal_left
print(double_times_decimal)

// Verifies the same conversion with the operand order reversed.
decimal_times_double: decimal = decimal_left * double_value
print(decimal_times_double)

<<< stdout
2.7000
2.7000

<<< stderr
